('multiple_choice','Anki-IPC-3262','A _____ route is a route to the network the interface is connected to. (Choose one answer)','["A. The prefix length configured on the interface.", "B. Gratuitous", "C. 40 seconds", "D. connected"]','[3]',NULL,10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'<div class="explanation-rich-content">\n  <div class="expl-card correct-card">\n    <h4 class="section-title-correct">✓ Correct Answer:</h4>\n    <p><strong>connected</strong></p>\n  </div>\n  <div class="expl-card concept-card">\n    <div class="section-title-concept">📌 Source: Anki Flashcards — IP Connectivity (CCNA / Day 11 (part 1) Flashcards - Routing Fundamentals)</div>\n  </div>\n</div>'),
('multiple_choice','Anki-IPC-3263','If a packet\'s destination IP is matched by multiple routes, which route will the router select? (Choose one answer)','["A. Exchange", "B. 2-way", "C. Active Virtual Forwarders (AVFs)", "D. The most specific matching route"]','[3]',NULL,10,NULL,NULL,NULL,'<div class="explanation-rich-content">\n  <div class="expl-card correct-card">\n    <h4 class="section-title-correct">✓ Correct Answer:</h4>\n    <p><strong>The most specific matching route</strong></p>\n  </div>\n  <div class="expl-card concept-card">\n    <div class="section-title-concept">📌 Source: Anki Flashcards — IP Connectivity (CCNA / Day 11 (part 1) Flashcards - Routing Fundamentals)</div>\n  </div>\n</div>'),
